# An Experimental Buchanan-Type Economics Course.

**Authors:** Page, A.N.

## Abstract
Describes the development and implementation of a Buchanan-type microeconomics course for first-year students in a Master of Business Administration program. The course is based on the recommendation of economist James Buchanan that economics should once again place its teaching emphasis on the various institutional arrangements that arise as a result of economic exchange. (Author/DB)

